{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1269574-most-useful-first-edition-books","id":1269574,"title":"Most useful first edition books?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-21T08:24:58-08:00","id":1269574,"title":"Most useful first edition books?","content":"I sorta mentioned this in my other thread, but just to give it its own subject: For a first time Mage ST, what are some of the better books to pick up to give you good inspiration for setting up a chronicle and building the setting for the players. Also what books are good for coming up with some early plot-lines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T08:45:35-08:00","id":1269580,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of Astral realms. I would say the order books are still fairly useful for setting content, if not mechanical content. Sanctum and Sigil is pretty good if you're looking for a more political game, while Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss and Night Horrors: The Unbidden are great if you're looking for something truly creepy/horrific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T09:10:08-08:00","id":1269584,"title":"","content":"Firstly,<i> Mage the Awakening</i> as a gameline has so much <i>stuff</i>, you and your players should just decide what you find most interesting and focus on that. Nobody should be expected to grasp everything at once.<br /> <br /> This thread may prove to be useful: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/mage-the-awakening-2e-seeking-advice-running-mage-for-the-first-time.815371/\" target=\"_blank\">LINK</a><br /> <br /> Although it's 1st Edition, the <i>Chronicler's Guide</i> has an entire chapter dedicated to storytelling advice. The remaining chapters describe rules hacks, and as such will be of less use to you.<br /> <br /> I'm seconding <i>Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss</i> and <i>Night Horrors: The Unbidden</i>. They're collections of antagonists and phenomena you can base your stories around. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar180_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"180\" data-vbnamecard=\"180\">Leliel</a> is doing an in-character &quot;Let's Read&quot; of the latter over at rpg.net: <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/cofd-sir-night-compiles-night-horrors-the-unbidden-in-character-lets-read.823385/\" target=\"_blank\">LINK</a><br /> <br /> <i>Left Hand Path</i> and <i>Seers of the Throne</i> describe factions of antagonistic mages, if you want to go in that direction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T09:33:52-08:00","id":1269588,"title":"","content":"Awesome, super helpful guys. I'm a total book completionist so I know if this catches on I'll probably end up getting everything the next time there's a decent drivethru sale. I guess I'm just trying to pick the order I read them in. Sounds like if I want to keep the horror tone Intruders and Night horrors is a good start from what you're saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T10:19:42-08:00","id":1269605,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm a fan I'd <i>Summoners</i>. If you want to add some flavour to your Supernal Beings, that's a great place to start. The Order books (including Seers) and Astral Realms I'd consider essential reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T10:29:03-08:00","id":1274904,"title":"","content":"My personal current top 3 favourites are:<br /> Sanctum and sigil. Describes mage society and more important cabals.<br /> Secrets of the ruined temple. About atlantean ruins, in short the indiana jones/tomb raider book.<br /> Keys to the supernal tarot. A lot of different things that I for some reason loves.<br /> Honourable mentions: Tome of the mysteries, summoners, astral realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T11:47:55-08:00","id":1274920,"title":"","content":"My vote would be for Left Hand Path. The fluff and mechanics on some of the more interesting villains is delicious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":